<section xml:id="section-first-order-odes" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>First-Order ODEs</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      An ordinary differential equation (ODE) relates an unknown function to
      its derivatives.
      This section develops the theory and solution methods for first-order
      ODEs, the most fundamental class.
      We begin by defining ODEs and clarifying what a solution is.
      We then study how to extract qualitative information from an ODE without
      solving it, using slope fields and sign arguments.
      Finally, we treat the two main solvable classes in full: separable ODEs
      (solved by integrating both sides after separating variables) and linear
      first-order ODEs (solved by the variation-of-constants formula).
      Throughout, engineering applications — population models, RC circuits —
      illustrate each concept.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <xi:include href="ode-introduction.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="qualitative-analysis.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="separable-odes.ptx"/>
  <xi:include href="linear-first-order-odes.ptx"/>

</section>
